! Silicon, 8 atoms in the conventional cubic cell, with an LDA ultrasoft pseudopotential.
!
! The reference for the ultrasoft path. ecutwfc is 20 Ry with a dual of 8, which is
! what the pseudopotential's own header suggests scaled to a test-sized run: the
! dual has to exceed 4 or the augmentation charge is not representable on the
! density grid, and it is exactly that separation of the two grids that the
! norm-conserving path never exercised.
!
! conv_thr is tightened far past what the answer needs so that both codes run to
! the same fixed point and the energy terms can be compared digit by digit.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=1, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=8, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0, ecutrho=160.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-n-rrkjus_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.00 0.50 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.00 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.50 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
 Si 0.25 0.75 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.25 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.75 0.25
K_POINTS
  1
   0.250000  0.250000  0.250000   1.00
